From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: musa <musa@local>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 11:11:24 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] MUSA: optimize hybrid attention page-size fastpath

Port of the vLLM-MUSA 0.28 series entry 0192 (PR #285) onto the 0.32.0 pin.

- Gather align-mode Mamba state block IDs with the MUSA JIT kernel instead of
  torch.gather, and reuse its stable buffer for non-speculative decode graphs.
- Keep the global scheduler block at the attention page when align mode puts
  Mamba state in a dedicated pool.
- Let the fused pre-copy context own ordinary align decode; stage postprocess
  inputs and resync accepted tokens only when a state block actually moved.

0.32 ships a multi-group aligned-index Triton gather for the MRV2 model-state
path, but the V1 GDN metadata builder still uses torch.gather and that kernel
asserts a CUDA device, so the MUSA kernel covers the V1 builder.
